License decision for local review candidate 0.1.0-rc.1

Report: "Neural Engine – Independent Research Report No. 001", copyright
2026 Eryk Wyrebek, is published independently under CC BY 4.0.
https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24492624
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Proposed, not yet granted: MIT for the original software (src/, experiments/
and tests/). It permits reuse and modification with attribution and is simple
for other laboratories to adopt. Review the standard text at
https://opensource.org/license/mit .

Proposed separately: CC BY 4.0 for the project-owned synthetic data,
configurations, checkpoints, results and documentation. This preserves
attribution when redistributing a benchmark separately from the software.

These proposals require the rights holder's explicit approval. This file
does not itself grant the proposed licenses. Before a public code/data
release, replace this notice with the approved texts, copyright notice
and a clear scope map. No third-party implementation, NumPy distribution
or article is relicensed by this proposal. Public access to the report
does not, by itself, license the software or research data.
